\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl202\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.  Give me the wings of faith to rise\cf0 
\par \pard\li225\sl202\slmult0\qj Within the veil, and see
\par The saints above, how great their joys,
\par \pard\li225\sl198\slmult0\qj How bright their glories be.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl198\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  Once they were mourners here below,
\par \pard\li225\sl198\slmult0 And poured out cries and tears;
\par They wrestled hard, as we do now,
\par With sins, and doubts, and fears.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl198\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  I ask them whence their victory came;
\par \pard\li225\sl198\slmult0 They, with united breath,
\par  Ascribe their conquest to the Lamb,
\par  Their triumph to His death.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li225\sl198\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  They marked the footsteps that He trod
\par \pard\li225\sl198\slmult0 His zeal inspired their breast;
\par  And, following their incarnate God,
\par Possess the promised rest.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li225\sl198\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Our glorious Leader claims our praise
\par \pard\li225\sl198\slmult0 For His own pattern given;
\par \pard\li225\sl202\slmult0 While the long cloud of witnesses
\par \pard      Show the same path to heaven.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

